.TH "PAYMENTRESPONSE.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PaymentResponse.toJSON \- PaymentResponse: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]PaymentResponse\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable plain
object representing the \f[CR]PaymentResponse\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]PaymentResponse\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]requestId\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]methodName\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]details\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]shippingAddress\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]shippingOption\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]payerName\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]payerEmail\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]payerPhone\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
When the returned object is passed to \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], the
\f[CR]shippingAddress\f[R] property is further serialized using
\f[CR]PaymentAddress.toJSON()\f[R] when it is not \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]PaymentResponse\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
payment.show().then((paymentResponse) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] json = paymentResponse.toJSON();
  console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
  console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
  console.log(json.methodName); \f[I]// Same value as paymentResponse.methodName\f[R]
});
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the callback from the previous example, the same object can be
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(paymentResponse));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqrequestId\(dq: \(dqcheckout\-123\(dq,
  \(dqmethodName\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/pay\(dq,
  \(dqdetails\(dq: {
    \(dqtransactionId\(dq: \(dq12345\(dq
  },
  \(dqshippingAddress\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqshippingOption\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqpayerName\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqpayerEmail\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqpayerPhone\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]JSON\f[R]
